the perimeter of the sector of the circle with a radius of 12, we need to consider the arc length and the two radii that form the sector. The sector is defined by a central angle of \\(60^\\circ\\).\n\n1. **Calculate the arc length:**\n   The formula for the arc length \\(L\\) of a sector with radius \\(r\\) and central angle \\(\\theta\\) (in degrees) is:\n   \\[\n   L = \\frac{\\theta}{360^\\circ} \\times 2\\pi r\n   \\]\n   Here, \\(r = 12\\) and \\(\\theta = 60^\\circ\\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n   \\[\n   L = \\frac{60^\\circ}{360^\\circ} \\times 2\\pi \\times 12 = \\frac{1}{6} \\times 24\\pi = 4\\pi\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the perimeter of the sector:**\n   The perimeter of the sector is the sum of the arc length and the two radii. So, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Perimeter} = L + 2r = 4\\pi + 2 \\times 12 = 4\\pi + 24\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the sector is \\(\\boxed{4\\pi + 24}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{4\\pi + 24}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:269"}
